Falsifies `rsext4::disknode::verification::extent_records_decode_reads_only_twelve_bytes`.

The defect: the extent decode reads `ee_start_lo` from bytes 9 to 12, one byte past the
twelve-byte record.

Expected to fail: the slice index in the extent decode.

diff --git a/src/disknode/disk_format.rs b/src/disknode/disk_format.rs
index f2a4f01..7c5c32a 100644
--- a/src/disknode/disk_format.rs
+++ b/src/disknode/disk_format.rs
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ impl DiskFormat for Ext4Extent {
             ee_block: read_u32_le(&bytes[0..4]),
             ee_len: read_u16_le(&bytes[4..6]),
             ee_start_hi: read_u16_le(&bytes[6..8]),
-            ee_start_lo: read_u32_le(&bytes[8..12]),
+            ee_start_lo: read_u32_le(&bytes[9..13]),
         }
     }
 
